// A member access on something that is not a bare name has no lowering.
//
// `a?.b` (safe navigation) is implemented: it lowers to OP_INDEX_GET and answers
// nil.  The plain form was not.  For an object that is not an EXPR_IDENT the
// EXPR_MEMBER case in src/compiler/compiler.c fell through to `return -1`, and
// every caller used that -1 as a register number -- so the program died with
// SIGSEGV at the first *use* of the value, while a bare statement was silently
// ignored:
//
//     say str(arr[0].bogus)   ->  RC=139   before the fix
//     arr[0].bogus            ->  RC=0     before the fix (silently dropped)
//
// This file is the red control for that fix.  It asserts the error, so it must
// never execute past the offending statement: the compiler refuses the file
// before the program starts.  If "must not be reached" ever prints, the
// compiler accepted a form it has no lowering for and the fix is gone.
//
// This is not a test of `?.`: that path already worked and is pinned by
// xrange_t2_v06.im's neighbour assertions.

arr = [1, 2]
say str(arr[0].bogus)
say "must not be reached"
